cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "PhysioTrack: contactless human sensing and body-signal extraction from RGB video"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  # TODO: add the remaining co-authors listed on the manuscript, with ORCIDs.
  - given-names: Tharindu
    family-names: Ekanayake
    email: physiotrack.ai@gmail.com
    affiliation: "Center for Machine Vision and Signal Analysis, University of Oulu"
repository-code: "https://github.com/tharindu326/physiotrack"
url: "https://tharindu326.github.io/physiotrack/"
abstract: >-
  PhysioTrack is an open-source Python library for contactless human sensing from
  monocular RGB video. It provides person and face detection, multi-object tracking,
  2D and 3D pose estimation with viewpoint canonicalization, face parsing and head
  orientation, body-part segmentation, monocular depth estimation, and extraction of
  physiological signals — remote photoplethysmography heart rate, heart-rate
  variability, and respiration — behind one unified predictor API.
keywords:
  - computer vision
  - human pose estimation
  - remote photoplethysmography
  - heart rate variability
  - respiration
  - physiological signals
  - monocular depth
  - multi-object tracking
  - biomechanics
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
